endobj
370 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 190 0 R
/E (We used four data mining models to study Amazon-style sales data. The classification model helped predict outcomes using labeled data but was less accurate than other methods. The regression model performed very well and predicted order totals with very small error. Clustering grouped customers into clear types, such as high spenders, budget shoppers, and average buyers. The association model showed that customers do not consistently buy the same items together, and most patterns were due to popular categories rather than strong product relationships. Together, these models gave a clear and complete picture of customer buying behavior.)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
371 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
